  "report_period": "Week 2 (3rd Jan to 10th Jan 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Kamsarmax \"Glory Prosperity\" 82/2007 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 07/2026, DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 11 mill. Note that the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Bettys Dream\" 82/2008 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 12/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold in December at USD 12,8 mill. SK Shipping have committed their Panamax \"K. Faith\" 75/2002 Sanoyas, Japan (SS 10/2027, DD 11/2025, BWTS fitted) to Chinese interests at USD 6,3 mill, while the Korean built \"Alpha Melody\" 74/2002 Daewoo, Korea (SS 05/2027, DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) of Alpha Bulkers Shipmanagement was committed at mid-high USD 6 mill. In addition, Target Marine committed their \"Mythos\" 74/2004 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 02/2029, DD 03/2027, BWTS fitted) at USD 8,6 mill. Remind you that back in November, the sister vessel \"Asia Graeca\" 73/2004 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 09/2029, DD 09/2027, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 11 mill. The Ultramax \"Omishima Island\" 61/2013 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 09/2025, BWTS fitted) of Shikishima Kisen was committed to clients of F-Maritime at mid-high USD 19 mill. For reference, the two-years-younger sister vessel \"Lowlands Amstel\" 61/2015 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold in late September at USD 26,3 mill. On the Supramax sector, C Transport Maritime SAM committed the \"CS Sonoma\" 56/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS 03/2025, DD 03/2026, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) at USD 11,4 mill. Remind you that the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Diva\" 56/2011 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 05/2026, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold back in September at USD 14,75 mill. One Shipping Denizcilik committed the vintage Handymax \"One Shine\" 46/2000 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted) at excess USD 5 mill. For comparison, the one-year-younger \"Rashad\" 48/2001 Sanoyas, Japan (SS 05/2026, DD 11/2024) was sold in November at USD 5,2 mill.",
    "tankers": "Kyklades Maritime committed the Aframax \"Nissos Delos\" 115/2012 Samsung, Korea (SS 08/2027, DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) to Bangladeshi interests at USD 45,3 mill. Remind you that the three-years-older \"Fos Da Vinci\" & \"Fos Picasso\" 115/2009 Samsung, Korea (SS 03/2029, DD 06/2027 & SS 07/2029, DD 06/2027, BWTS fitted) were committed back in October at USD 42 mill each.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 8,000/10,000 pd range. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 4,000/7,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 4,000/7,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 9,000/10,000 pd. West Coast Indian trips into China were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. West Coast Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 8,000/11,000 pd. South African trips into India were fixed around usd 11,000/12,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 100K. South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 13,000/15,000 pd. South American trips into US East Coast were fixed around usd 15,000 pd plus ballast at the usd 100K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 10,500 pd for 5/8 months employment basis delivery China.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 4,000/6,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 10,000 pd. South African trips into Arabian Gulf were reported at the level of usd 9,000/11,000 pd. South African trips into China were fixed around usd 10,000/11,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 100K/110K. US Gulf trips into China were reported at the level of usd 17,000/19,000 pd. US Gulf trips into South America were fixed around usd 15,000/16,000 pd. Trips from US East Coast into Continent were reported at the level of usd 19,000/21,000 pd. On the period front, an Ultramax was reported fixed in the usd 10,750 pd for 3/5 months employment basis delivery West Coast India.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of Australian trips into China with logs were fixed around usd 9,000/10,000 pd. Trips from Singapore via Thailand into Indonesia were reported at the level of usd 7,000/8,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into North Coast South America were fixed around usd 13,000/14,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
